{"name":"Sea Sprite","hex":"#b7ccc7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"},{"term":"sprite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various supernatural beings, loosely defined:\nA spirit; a soul; a shade.\n\nAn apparition; a ghost.\nAn elf, fairy, or goblin; one with a small humanlike physical body.","A spirit; a soul; a shade."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To draw a (specifically) pixel art sprite."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sprite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sprite (folklore)","blocks":[{"text":"A sprite is a supernatural entity in European mythology. Sprites are often depicted as fairy-like creatures or as ethereal entities."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sprite_(folklore)"},{"title":"Sea Sprite Sailing Yachts","blocks":[{"text":"Sea Sprite sailing yachts is a family of US built sailing vessels. The series includes the following yachts, a 23', 28', 30', and a 34'. They were all simply designated Sea Sprites. The twin sails in a following seas emblem is well known in the yachting world."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_Sprite_Sailing_Yachts"},{"title":"Sprite (lightning)","blocks":[{"text":"Sprites or red sprites are large-scale electric discharges that occur in the mesosphere, high above thunderstorm clouds, or cumulonimbus, giving rise to a varied range of visual shapes flickering in the night sky. They are usually triggered by the discharges of positive lightning between an underlying thundercloud and the ground."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Sprite_over_Southeast_Asia_from_ISS.jpg/330px-Sprite_over_Southeast_Asia_from_ISS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sprite_(lightning)"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Richard_Doyle_-_Spurned_Suitor.jpg/330px-Richard_Doyle_-_Spurned_Suitor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Richard_Doyle_-_Spurned_Suitor.jpg/330px-Richard_Doyle_-_Spurned_Suitor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The prince thanking the Water sprite, from The Princess Nobody: A Tale of Fairyland (1884) by Andrew Lang (illustration by Richard Doyle)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARichard_Doyle_-_Spurned_Suitor.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/August_Malmstr%C3%B6m_-_Dancing_Fairies_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-August_Malmstr%C3%B6m_-_Dancing_Fairies_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/August_Malmstr%C3%B6m_-_Dancing_Fairies_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/1280px-August_Malmstr%C3%B6m_-_Dancing_Fairies_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/August_Malmstr%C3%